WEBVTT

00:00:01,360 --> 00:00:06,040
No, this is for my grandkids, and it's Grandpa's story.

00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:12,370
There's a buzz in the air.

00:00:12,370 --> 00:00:14,330
There's a buzz in the air.

00:00:14,330 --> 00:00:16,610
It's a bee over there.

00:00:16,610 --> 00:00:20,810
It's just above it Helen's big fluffy hair.

00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:24,850
It's flying around Chuck in the old wooden chair.

00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:31,270
It landed on April, and she fainted right there.

00:00:31,270 --> 00:00:40,670
The buzz passed the swing set, and over the fence, just a circle again, how it doesn't make sense.

00:00:40,670 --> 00:00:44,910
He's spoiling our picnic and scaring the baby.

00:00:44,910 --> 00:00:52,460
He whizzed past the table right over the gravy.

00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:57,980
Round the tree, here he comes, with more speed than a car.

00:00:57,980 --> 00:01:02,660
Close your mouth, squint your eyes, for he's not very far.

00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:07,780
Zoom, he goes faster than I can keep up this riddle.

00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:16,710
Look, he split Johnny's part in his hair, down the middle.

00:01:16,710 --> 00:01:26,070
There's a buzz in the air, and he's flying by Pa, who's cutting grass with the lawn more chewing up son.

00:01:26,070 --> 00:01:30,350
Run in the house, or hide under a rock.

00:01:30,350 --> 00:01:38,400
I think the buzz has just summoned his flock.

00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:47,480
He's after the watermelon, or something more, grab the chips, the cupcakes, and head for the door.

00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:52,360
Susie just screamed, and plopped down in her chair.

00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:59,500
A mother was tempted to leave her right there.

00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:10,260
Grandma's dress turned all red from the drink that Sam spilled, and she jumped and tipped over the jello while chilled.

00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:13,620
That it bounced off Anne's face.

00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:19,340
On her nose left some cream, then proceeded to splat on her lap.

00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:23,470
Oh, some cream.

00:02:23,470 --> 00:02:26,030
There's a buzz in the air.

00:02:26,030 --> 00:02:28,550
He just flew around the corner.

00:02:28,550 --> 00:02:36,670
We thought that we were all through with the horror, but no sooner could Anne cleat off her pants.

00:02:36,670 --> 00:02:41,310
Then I looked up to see one giant army of Anne's.

